# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each exclusion below is here for a stated reason. A later edit that removes one
# should remove the reasoning too, or it is removing a guardrail by accident.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# THE ATHLETE'S PRIVATE WORKSPACE.
# Health data, clinical correspondence, blood work, cycle tracking, body
# composition, and anything a clinician has said. This does not belong in a git
# repository at any level of the tree — not in the corpus, and not in the
# registers either. The registers may record THAT a referral exists; never what
# it found.
advisory/private/

# THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL HELD FOR PERSONAL USE.
# Books, purchased training plans, paid course material, gated coaching content.
# ip_class: licensed in SCHEMA.md — it may shape a training decision and must
# never reach anything outward-facing, including by paraphrase. Distillations of
# it that live in advisory/kb/ ARE tracked; the source material is not.
advisory/sources/
*.epub
*.mobi
*.azw3
/*.pdf

# RAW TRAINING EXPORTS.
# GPX, FIT and TCX files, and platform CSV dumps. Binary, enormous, do not diff,
# and their home is the platform that produced them. Derived figures in
# advisory/analysis/ are tracked; the exports are not.
advisory/exports/
*.fit
*.gpx
*.tcx

# RUN OUTPUT.
# Per-node notes from an advisory run. Working artifacts: read them, act on them,
# let them regenerate. They are never the record.
advisory/.run-notes/
advisory/kb/.ingest-notes/

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS and editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
